    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute over trip TRP-02826 is escalated to a human reviewer. No money moves now — the SGD 26.73 charge stands, the disputed SGD 11.00 is held rather than refunded or collected, and I issue no refund and no driver compensation.\n\nThe reason is the GPS trace. The POL-RD-01 route-deviation test runs on EV-GPS-02826, and that trace is impaired at both levels. It carries weight_multiplier 0.6 with issue code GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW: a 100.0-second gap between fixes, from 19:39:44 to 19:41:24, with the two bounding fixes 1.01 km apart, on a trace sampled every 10 seconds (174 fixes, 94.5% coverage). A gap over 90 seconds is impairment under POL-RD-07(a), so the trace is impaired for policy purposes as well as at schema level, and I say both things as POL-GEN-02(3) and POL-RD-07 require.\n\nThe figures. EV-GPS-02826 measures the driven route at 18.2 km; EV-TRIP-02826 records the booked optimal route at 14.0 km (19.0 minutes); the excess is 4.2 km, or 30.0% of optimal. That would clear both POL-RD-01 limbs (over 20% and over 0.8 km). On the fare side, EV-FARE-02826 (weight 1.0) shows charged_total SGD 26.73, fare model METERED, surge_multiplier 1.0 read from the fare breakdown and nowhere else, no ERP and no airport surcharge. Had the deviation been established, POL-RD-02 would give recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 19.0) x 1.0) + 0.80 platform fee = SGD 20.42, and a refund of 26.73 - 20.42 = 6.31, rounded up to SGD 6.35 — above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and below the 90% full-refund share. Both advocates ran exactly this arithmetic and it is correct; I do not issue it, because escalation is terminal and replaces any monetary outcome.\n\nWhy the deviation cannot be established. Under POL-RD-07(ii) an impaired trace cannot establish a deviation alone; an independent source is required. Going through the clause's list: the chat log (EV-CHAT-02826) holds 0 messages, so there is no admission there; the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02826) has 0 ERP lines and the trace carries no erp_gantries, so no off-corridor gantry places the vehicle; the trip record's 18.2 km is, by POL-RD-01's own words, a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement and so is not independent; and the fare breakdown's billed 18.2 km is a copy of the trace figure — I checked, and it is exactly the trace figure — which POL-RD-07 states is not independent corroboration. That answers the driver's claim that the billed distance independently corroborates the excess: it is the same measurement in a second artifact, and it corroborates nothing.\n\nThe one remaining candidate is the driver's counterparty statement, 'Navigation rerouted me.' That is a bare assertion of an external cause: it names no road, no segment and no route, and POL-RD-13 tests such an assertion against the traffic advisory and nothing else. No advisory is on file — EV-ADVIS-02826-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, and nothing covers the Blk 108 Yishun Ring Rd corridor in this window — so the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08 and is no POL-RD-03 exoneration. To be complete: even reading the statement at its highest, as a counterparty statement that admits a reroute and so meets the corroboration limb of POL-RD-07(ii), it decides that limb and no more. It carries no weight_multiplier, so under POL-GEN-02(2) it enters neither the minimum nor the maximum of the confidence cap, and the deciding fact — an excess of 4.2 km — is carried by EV-GPS-02826 alone at weight 0.6.\n\nTriggers. POL-RD-10(1) fires: my confidence cannot exceed 0.6, the weight of the only artifact carrying the deciding fact, which is below the 0.70 confidence_floor read from the loaded policy. POL-RD-10(3) also fires: the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a) and no corroborating artifact of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names exists. Absence of proof here is a data failure, not a finding for the driver, so the outcome is ESCALATE and not NO_ACTION; and because the impaired trace is the only evidence, the finding does not survive the 0.6 discount under POL-GEN-02(3). The monetary effect would have been SGD 6.35, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, but escalation is terminal and nothing executes.\n\nWhat would resolve it: an independent measurement of this trip's route — a platform or rider-side GPS export of TRP-02826, or the ERP gantry records for the trip window; a chat log for the trip if one exists beyond the empty EV-CHAT-02826; or a traffic advisory covering this window, which would let a POL-RD-03 comparison be run. Any of those would let the POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 arithmetic be carried to a final monetary ruling.\n\nThe claims, and how they stand. (1) Both sides' points that POL-RD-04 is unavailable because the chat log is empty (EV-CHAT-02826, 0 messages): accepted — there is no rider instruction, no timestamp and no waypoint_hint, so no distance is excluded on that ground. (2) Both sides' points that POL-RD-05 cannot be run: accepted — pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at, original_pickup, original_dropoff and amended_optimal_distance_km are all null on EV-TRIP-02826, so the booked 14.0 km stands as the baseline. (3) The driver's POL-RD-12 point (vehicle_type RYDE_X, solo_optimal_distance_km null): accepted — no matched-itinerary baseline is in play. (4) The driver's POL-RD-11 point (fare model METERED, quoted_fare_sgd null): accepted — POL-RD-11 does not close off the distance-and-time route, and POL-RD-02 would govern if the finding could be made. (5) Both sides' POL-RD-02 computations (recomputed_fare 20.42, refund 6.31 rounded to 6.35, PARTIAL_REFUND): the arithmetic is accepted, but the finding it depends on cannot be made on this record, so it is outweighed by the escalation; the figures are set out above so both parties can see what the money would have been. (6) The driver's claim that EV-FARE-02826's distance_charged_km is independent corroboration: rejected, for the reason given — it is a copy of the trace figure. (7) The rider's claim that the trace figure governs under POL-RD-01: accepted as to which field governs, but an impaired trace cannot be the sole basis of the finding. (8) Both sides' POL-RD-06 points (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d 0 over completed_trips_90d 287, no pattern): accepted — no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter (1) is context only under POL-GEN-01; both claims mention it only to say it may not be substituted, which is right, and I have not used it. (9) Both sides' POL-RD-08 points (rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d 0, deviation_claims_60d_substantiated 0): accepted — the rider's claim carries no extra corroboration requirement from that profile. (10) Both sides' POL-RD-09 points (0 ERP lines, 0 tolls, 0 airport surcharge on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport): accepted — no pass-through correction and no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral. (11) The rider's payment-status point (CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.0): moot now, since the amount is held rather than refunded.\n\nNo referral issues. A referral must be produced by a clause: POL-RD-06(c) needs a repeat-deviation pattern (none), POL-RD-09(4) needs a phantom or unmatched charge line (there is none), and POL-NS-05(ii) and POL-NS-07 do not apply to a route-deviation case. The nine claims the referee struck were struck for citing impaired artifacts without disclosing the impairment; that is the code's check, those entries appear in the discarded list, and I have relied on none of them."
  },
