    "explanation": "This ruling is addressed to both parties. No money changes hands today: the case escalates to a human reviewer, and the disputed amount is held — not collected again and not refunded — until that review.\n\nThe distance picture. Trip TRP-02826 was booked on a 14.0 km optimal route and was driven 18.2 km, an excess of 4.2 km, which is 30.0% of optimal (EV-TRIP-02826; EV-GPS-02826). That clears both POL-RD-01 establishment limbs (over 20% and over 0.8 km) and is not a MATERIAL deviation (under 50% and under 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 profile uplift is not engaged. Had a refund been issuable, POL-RD-02 on this METERED fare (surge 1.0, read from EV-FARE-02826) would give: charged_total 26.73; recomputed_fare 20.42 = (3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 19.0) x 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP; refund 26.73 - 20.42 = 6.31, rounded up to 6.35. I am not issuing it.\n\nWhy no ruling issues. The route is measured only by EV-GPS-02826, and that trace is impaired. The admissibility pre-pass tagged it GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW — a 100.0 s sampling gap from 19:39:44 to 19:41:24, 1.01 km apart in a straight line — at weight_multiplier 0.6, and the policy test fires as well, because a gap of more than 90 seconds meets POL-RD-07(a). It is therefore impaired at schema level and for policy purposes. Under POL-RD-07(ii) the deviation cannot be established on the trace alone; it needs one of the independent sources that clause names, and none is on this record: the chat log is empty (EV-CHAT-02826, 0 messages, no driver admission), no ERP gantry was charged (0 ERP lines, erp_gantries empty), and the trip record's 18.2 km and the fare breakdown's billed 18.2 km are copies of the same trace measurement — POL-RD-01 calls the trip-record figure a rounded convenience copy, and POL-RD-07(ii) says billed distance is not independent corroboration where it is a copy. The driver's statement 'Navigation rerouted me' is an assertion of an external cause citing no advisory; the advisory for this trip is MISSING (EV-ADVIS-02826-01, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-RD-03 cannot run, and under POL-RD-13 such an assertion is tested against the traffic_advisory and nothing else, so it carries no weight under POL-RD-08 — it neither reduces the excess nor supplies an amended optimal route.\n\nThe triggers that fired. POL-RD-10(3): the gps_trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) and no corroborating artifact of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names exists. POL-RD-10(1), independently: the deciding distance fact rests solely on an artifact at weight 0.6, so confidence cannot exceed 0.6, below the 0.70 platform floor (POL-GEN-02(2)). What would resolve it: a record independent of this trace — a driver admission in the chat log, an ERP gantry record placing the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use, a counterparty statement that actually admits the route driven, or a re-exported GPS trace without the 100-second gap.\n\nThe advocates' claims. The arithmetic claims from both sides (a 6.35 refund on a METERED fare; nothing added for ERP under POL-RD-09) are correct as arithmetic but are outrun by the escalation, which is terminal and replaces any monetary outcome. The driver's claim that the fare breakdown's billed distance is independent corroboration is rejected: it is a copy of the trace figure, which POL-RD-07(ii) expressly excludes. Both sides' profile claims are accepted: deviation_flags_90d of 0 across 287 completed trips shows no repeat-deviation pattern, so there is no POL-RD-06(b) FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used. The claims that POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05, POL-RD-11 and POL-RD-12 are unavailable are accepted on the record (no chat instruction, no amended endpoints, METERED and not UPFRONT_QUOTE, RYDE_X and not RYDE_POOL). There is no ERP, toll, airport-surcharge or other unmatched charge line, so no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral arises and the referrals list is empty. Claims that cited the impaired trace or the absent advisory without disclosing the impairment were set aside by the mechanical citation check and carried no weight."
  },
